>Could this not be abstracted to include any comodity, including money,
>gold, corn, single crystals of Si, Drugs, Guns, MIP-years, or labor?  Each
>pair of comodities would then have a relative intrest rate, with competative
>markets in each.  For those of you who have not figured out what
>denominating contracts in goods would do, think about taxation and
>inflation:-)
